[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_dlg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_dlg")
source = "# Vesper: Null Speaker, guide to the Core (Acts IV and V). Calm, eerie.
~ start
@ quest_active:q06c_root_access -> out_of_quarantine
@ quest_ready:q08_null_gatekeeper -> ready_q08_null_gatekeeper
@ quest_ready:null_fragments -> ready_fragments
@ quest_ready:q07_null_weaver_prime -> ready_q07_null_weaver_prime
@ quest_ready:q07a_learn_the_language -> ready_language
@ can_start:q07a_learn_the_language -> offer_language
@ can_start:q07_null_weaver_prime -> offer_q07_null_weaver_prime
@ can_start:q08_null_gatekeeper -> offer_q08_null_gatekeeper
@ can_start:null_fragments -> offer_fragments
@ quest_ready:under_new_rules -> ready_rules
@ can_start:under_new_rules -> offer_rules
@ quest_active:q08_null_gatekeeper -> remind_q08_null_gatekeeper
@ quest_active:q07_null_weaver_prime -> remind_q07_null_weaver_prime
@ quest_active:q07a_learn_the_language -> remind_language
@ quest_active:null_fragments -> remind_fragments
@ quest_active:under_new_rules -> remind_rules
@ deed:ending:any -> after_ending
@ quest_done:q10_root_process -> before_choice
@ quest_active:q10_root_process -> during_root
@ quest_active:q09_core_sentinel -> during_sentinel
@ quest_done:q08_null_gatekeeper -> at_the_core
-> idle

~ offer_language
Vesper: You can hear it, can’t you? The Null speaks. You just never listened.
Vesper: The Weavers speak in patterns. Break them and you’ll hear the grammar.
* ACCEPT -> accept_language
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_language
> start_quest q07a_learn_the_language
Vesper: Out there it rewrites AXIOM's rules, one at a time. Bring a script set for each. I'll meet you at The Fray.
Vesper: Don’t fear them. Read them.
-> end

~ remind_language
Vesper: Six of them, in The Fray. Watch the gaps in what they fire.
-> end

~ ready_language
Vesper: Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_language
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_language
> turn_in q07a_learn_the_language
Vesper: You see it now. The Null has syntax. It has logic.
-> start

~ offer_fragments
Vesper: Some Weavers carry pieces of what they’re saying. Five, in The Fray. I want to read them together.
* ACCEPT -> accept_fragments
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_fragments
> start_quest null_fragments
Vesper: Careful. They’re unstable. So was everyone who tried to read them.
-> end

~ remind_fragments
Vesper: Five fragments. Bring me all of them, or it’s only noise.
-> end

~ ready_fragments
Vesper: Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_fragments
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_fragments
> turn_in null_fragments
Vesper: It’s not destruction. It’s a message. A very old one.
Vesper: It isn’t addressed to the Null. It’s addressed to whoever gets there first.
-> start

~ at_the_core
Vesper: The way is open. What you do next is yours alone.
-> end

~ during_sentinel
Vesper: The Stack Trace is full of things you've already killed. The Core keeps everything.
Vesper: Don't let it make you fight the past the same way twice.
-> end

~ during_root
Vesper: The Root Process isn't evil. It's the last thing in AXIOM that still believes the old rules.
-> end

~ before_choice
Vesper: It's quiet. I've never heard the Null this quiet. It's waiting for you.
-> end

~ after_ending
Vesper: Whatever you chose, you chose it awake. That's more than the Architects did.
-> end

~ offer_rules
Vesper: You keep fighting its laws. Stop. Fight under them.
Vesper: Win once under every law it writes, and you'll understand it better than the Guild ever did.
* ACCEPT -> accept_rules
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_rules
> start_quest under_new_rules
Vesper: Six under each. Out in the Null Zone, where the laws run. Bring a script set for each one.
-> end

~ remind_rules
Vesper: Six kills under each of its laws. The banner tells you which one you're under.
-> end

~ ready_rules
> turn_in under_new_rules
Vesper: You did it its way. How did it feel?
Vesper: Don't answer. I could see it. You looked like you belonged out there.
-> end

~ out_of_quarantine
Vesper: Eleven days of listening. It hasn't stopped calling. It's calling you.
Vesper: The copy had no Executor in it. It can copy any process, but not one that rewrites itself.
-> end

~ offer_q07_null_weaver_prime
Vesper: The Weaver spins the Null’s grammar. Break it and you’ll hear the language.
* ACCEPT -> accept_q07_null_weaver_prime
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_q07_null_weaver_prime
> start_quest q07_null_weaver_prime
Vesper: Don’t fear it. Read it.
-> end

~ remind_q07_null_weaver_prime
# NEW line below
Vesper: Read the pattern. Step through the gaps.

~ ready_q07_null_weaver_prime
Vesper: Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_q07_null_weaver_prime
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_q07_null_weaver_prime
> turn_in q07_null_weaver_prime
Vesper: You see it now. The Null has logic. It isn’t just destruction.
Vesper: One thing still stands between you and the Core. Sudo will want a word first.
-> start

~ offer_q08_null_gatekeeper
Vesper: The Gatekeeper guards the Core. It will not let you pass.
* ACCEPT -> accept_q08_null_gatekeeper
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_q08_null_gatekeeper
> start_quest q08_null_gatekeeper
Vesper: Prove your code is worthy. Sudo will test you first. The road opens when you pass.
-> end

~ remind_q08_null_gatekeeper
# NEW line below
Vesper: Sudo first. Then the Gate. Take its key, and go through.

~ ready_q08_null_gatekeeper
Vesper: Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_q08_null_gatekeeper
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_q08_null_gatekeeper
> turn_in q08_null_gatekeeper
Vesper: The way is open. What you do next is yours alone.
-> start

~ idle
Vesper: Listen. The silence has structure."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dd85gxidfhqxl"
